  "id": "COMPOUND:1938 - PROTEIN:522",
  "verbalization": "N-[3-(aminomethyl)benzyl]acetamidine is implicated in the biological pathway leading to Threonine--tRNA ligase, mitochondrial, through a series of interconnected targets. The drug is directly linked to Gamma-butyrobetaine dioxygenase, which is a target of Imidazole and N-(4-{2-[(3-chlorobenzyl)amino]ethyl}phenyl)thiophene-2-carboximidamide. This latter compound, in turn, targets Threonine--tRNA ligase, mitochondrial. The evidence suggests that N-[3-(aminomethyl)benzyl]acetamidine may act as a modulator of the metabolic pathway involving Gamma-butyrobetaine dioxygenase, potentially influencing the activity of Threonine--tRNA ligase, mitochondrial. The presence of multiple pathways converging on this target indicates a possible role for the drug in regulating mitochondrial function through the intermediary of Gamma-butyrobetaine dioxygenase. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which N-[3-(aminomethyl)benzyl]acetamidine could influence mitochondrial processes, though the exact nature of its interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
